## 2 & 3. Reading a file, then parsing it

`readFileSync` hands back **text**, not data. It has no idea the file contains JSON — it would read a
CSV or a log file identically. The `"utf-8"` argument matters: without it you get raw bytes.

```ts
import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";
const text = readFileSync("./data.json", "utf-8");
const data = JSON.parse(text);
```

